From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:41:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Pass over an element without styles when viewport units
 are invalidated

An element can carry style data before it has styles: an embedder may
set up its data when it creates the element (Blitz does), and the
traversal never styles an element under `display: none`. A viewport
resize walked every element with data and asked each for its
`viewport_unit_usage`, which unwraps the primary style, so a document
that uses viewport units panicked when resized while it held such an
element.

Such an element needs no invalidation of its own: the next traversal
that reaches it styles it from scratch. The walk still goes on into its
children, which can be styled (a subtree moved under it) and use
viewport units. The stylesheet invalidator already passes over an
element without styles the same way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 style/invalidation/viewport_units.rs | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/style/invalidation/viewport_units.rs b/style/invalidation/viewport_units.rs
index 06faeb14c..4fc903578 100644
--- a/style/invalidation/viewport_units.rs
+++ b/style/invalidation/viewport_units.rs
@@ -33,7 +33,16 @@ where
         return false;
     }
 
-    let usage = data.styles.viewport_unit_usage();
+    // An element can carry data before it has styles: an embedder may set up
+    // its data when it creates the element, and the traversal does not style
+    // an element under `display: none`. The next traversal that reaches it
+    // styles it from scratch, so it needs no invalidation of its own, but
+    // its descendants can be styled (a subtree moved under it) and may.
+    let usage = if data.has_styles() {
+        data.styles.viewport_unit_usage()
+    } else {
+        ViewportUnitUsage::None
+    };
     let uses_viewport_units = usage != ViewportUnitUsage::None;
     if uses_viewport_units {
         debug!(
